at is the range of the function $h$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $-5$ | $-\\frac{2}{5}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $3$ | $4$ | $\\frac{9}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $h(x)$ | $\\frac{9}{2}$ | $4$ | $3$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-\\frac{2}{5}$ | $-5$ |" :question/worked-solution "The range of $f(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $h(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-5,-\\frac{2}{5},0,1,\\frac{3}{2},3,4,\\frac{9}{2}\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d3796fa-e911-5553-83c2-24c98370e4ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Function's Range From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "066fe7e7-8e26-541f-8b62-8fd28458ef00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546262} {:answer/id #uuid "366b1806-7914-5cb1-942b-dec36c098f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546369} {:answer/id #uuid "5a85aea4-e173-5173-98f5-fc005c6b3a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546449} {:answer/id #uuid "99dff75f-e3f4-5977-a145-8d4f732f4e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-\\frac{5}{2},-\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546593} {:answer/id #uuid "a2638e78-5940-53d1-83f6-32278bd799ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{